

== Presentation of Barid Al-Maghrib

Barid Al-Maghrib (BAM) is the national postal operator of the Kingdom of Morocco. It is responsible for ensuring the provision of postal services across the entire national territory, within the framework of universal service obligations defined by Moroccan legislation. Over time, the institution has evolved from a traditional postal administration into a diversified group offering logistics, financial, and digital services.

=== Historical Background

The origins of postal services in Morocco date back to the end of the nineteenth century. The first structured postal organization was established by royal decree in 1892, marking the beginning of a formalized communication system within the country @bam_history @wiki_bam.

During the Protectorate period, postal, telegraph, and telephone services were reorganized following European administrative models. In 1912, the Administration Chérifienne des Postes, des Télégraphes et des Téléphones was created and became responsible for managing national postal and telecommunications operations. The same year saw the issuance of the first Moroccan postage stamp, symbolizing the institutionalization of postal services @bam_history.

After independence in 1956, postal and telecommunications services were integrated under the supervision of the Ministry of Posts, Telegraphs and Telephones. This period was characterized by efforts to extend postal coverage to rural areas and strengthen national infrastructure.

In 1984, the Office National des Postes et des Télécommunications (ONPT) was created, centralizing postal and telecommunications activities within a single public entity @onpt.

A major reform occurred with the promulgation of Law 24-96, which reorganized the communications sector in Morocco. This law led to the separation of postal and telecommunications activities and established Barid Al-Maghrib as an autonomous public institution with legal and financial independence @law2496.

In 2010, Barid Al-Maghrib was transformed into a state-owned limited company (société anonyme), reinforcing its managerial autonomy while maintaining full public ownership. This transformation was accompanied by the consolidation of financial activities under Al Barid Bank @wiki_bam.

=== Missions of Barid Al-Maghrib

Barid Al-Maghrib is entrusted with ensuring universal postal service coverage throughout Morocco. Its missions are defined by Law 24-96 and include the collection, sorting, transportation, and distribution of postal items at both national and international levels @law2496.

More specifically, BAM is responsible for:

- Providing universal postal services across all regions;
- Managing domestic and international mail and parcel flows;
- Operating express mail and logistics services;
- Contributing to financial inclusion through postal financial services;
- Supporting e-government and digital transformation initiatives;
- Ensuring compliance with international postal agreements.

These missions place BAM at the intersection of public service obligations and competitive logistics markets, requiring a balance between accessibility, affordability, and operational efficiency.

=== Organizational Structure

Barid Al-Maghrib is structured as a hierarchical organization governed by a Board of Directors responsible for defining strategic orientations and approving major investment and development plans.

Operational management is ensured by executive directorates covering core functions such as:

- Postal operations and logistics;
- Information systems and digital transformation;
- Finance and accounting;
- Human resources management;
- Commercial and customer services.

The operational network is distributed across regional directorates, sorting centers, and post offices, ensuring nationwide coverage. This decentralized structure enables the institution to maintain proximity to users while coordinating large-scale logistics operations.

The governance framework of BAM is defined by Law 24-96 and subsequent regulatory texts governing public enterprises in Morocco @law2496.

=== Postal Activities

Historically, postal services constituted the core activity of Barid Al-Maghrib. While traditional letter mail has declined due to digital communication, parcel and logistics activities have experienced strong growth, driven mainly by the expansion of e-commerce.

The main postal products include:

- Ordinary mail and printed matter;
- Registered mail with tracking capabilities;
- Express Mail Service (EMS);
- Domestic and international parcels;
- Post office boxes and address-related services.

International parcel flows in particular have become a strategic activity due to increasing trade exchanges and diaspora-related shipments. These services require strong coordination between operational, customs, and transportation systems.

=== Subsidiaries and Group Structure

Barid Al-Maghrib has developed a group structure to diversify its activities and respond to evolving market demands.

The most important subsidiary is Al Barid Bank, created in 2010 to consolidate postal financial services and promote financial inclusion in Morocco. Leveraging BAM's extensive territorial network, Al Barid Bank provides banking services to individuals and small businesses across the country @wiki_bam.

Other affiliated entities operate in logistics, express delivery, and media services, contributing to the diversification of the group’s revenue sources and strengthening its position in competitive markets.

=== International Cooperation

Barid Al-Maghrib is a member of the Universal Postal Union (UPU), a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for coordinating international postal exchanges and establishing global postal standards @upu.

Through this membership, Morocco participates in a global postal network that enables the exchange of mail with more than 180 countries. The UPU framework defines operational rules governing:

- International dispatch preparation;
- Customs documentation;
- Tracking and electronic data exchange;
- Compensation between postal operators.

Compliance with these standards ensures interoperability between national postal systems and improves the reliability of cross-border postal flows.

=== Challenges and Strategic Orientation

Like many postal operators worldwide, Barid Al-Maghrib faces structural challenges related to the decline of traditional mail volumes and the rapid growth of parcel logistics driven by e-commerce.

Key challenges include:

- Increasing variability in international shipment volumes;
- Modernization of legacy information systems;
- Optimization of transportation and sorting capacities;
- Improvement of shipment traceability and data quality;
- Integration of data-driven decision-making tools.

To address these challenges, BAM has engaged in a strategic transformation process focused on digitalization, operational efficiency, and service diversification. The exploitation of data and predictive analytics has become increasingly important in supporting planning and decision-making processes.

In this context, the present internship contributes to the broader objective of enhancing operational intelligence through the analysis and forecasting of Morocco's outgoing international mail flows.